/nam-tok-food"],["Pad see ew","dish/pad-see-ew"],["Pad thai","dish/pad-thai"],["Rad naa","dish/rad-naa"],["Rice noodle roll","dish/rice-noodle-roll"],["Sorn (restaurant)","dish/sorn-restaurant"],["Sweet chili sauce","dish/sweet-chili-sauce"],["Thai curry","dish/thai-curry"],["Thai Express","dish/thai-express"],["Thai fried rice","dish/thai-fried-rice"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Thua nao","dish/thua-nao"],["Tom kha kai","dish/tom-kha-kai"],["Tom yum","dish/tom-yum"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/60/PaaDee%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon_%282022%29_-_2.jpg/500px-PaaDee%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon_%282022%29_-_2.jpg","w":500,"h":281,"by":"Another Believer","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PaaDee%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon_(2022)_-_2.jpg"}},"dish/picanteria":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/picanteria","n":"Picantería","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Peruvian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A picantería, is a traditional lunchtime restaurant in Peru, predominantly in and around the cities of Arequipa and Cuzco. Typical offerings of Arequipan cuisine include chicha corn beer made out of a locally grown black corn called Guinapo.  Meanwhile in the north of Peru they make chicha de Jora which is germinated corn. Dishes include \"Chupes\", more stews than soups, which have a designated day of the week. Picanteria refers to a place serving  picante (\"spicy\"), a one-plate dish of various stews."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-picanteria"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picanter%C3%ADa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Peruvian cuisine","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Peru Delights","ref":"site/perudelights-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"perudelights.com","note":"Morena Cuadra's blog of Peruvian home recipes and food culture.","url":"https://perudelights.com/tag/peruvian-home-cooking/","suggested":true},{"name":"Eat Peru","ref":"site/eatperu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"eatperu.com","note":"Guide to Peruvian dishes and ingredients with a recipe section.","url":"https://www.eatperu.com/category/recipes/?sf_paged=2","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Peruvian cuisine","links":[["Andina (restaurant)","dish/andina-restaurant"],["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Central (restaurant)","dish/central-restaurant"],["Chicha morada","dish/chicha-morada"],["Coca tea","dish/coca-tea"],["La Rosa Náutica","dish/la-rosa-nautica"],["Lima (restaurant)","dish/lima-restaurant"],["Locro","dish/locro"],["Maido (restaurant)","dish/maido-restaurant"],["Peruvian ceviche","dish/peruvian-ceviche"],["Picarones","dish/picarones"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e1/Picanteria_las_Paraguitas.jpg/500px-Picanteria_las_Paraguitas.jpg","w":500,"h":376,"by":"Ordzonhyd Rudyard Tarco Palomino","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Picanteria_las_Paraguitas.jpg"}},"dish/pie-and-mash":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pie-and-mash","n":"Pie and mash","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from English cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pie and mash is a British working-class food, originating in the docks of London, considered \"a Cockney classic\". It typically consists of a minced beef pie (formerly also eel pie) served with mashed potato and a parsley sauce known as liquor, with malt vinegar or non-brewed condiment (similar to vinegar) as a condiment. Pie and mash shops have been in London since the 19th century and are still common in East and South London, as well as many parts of Kent and Essex."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pie-and-mash"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie_and_mash"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Mashed potatoes","ingredient/mashed-potatoes"],["Parsley sauce","ingredient/parsley-sauce"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"]]},{"h":"More from English cuisine","links":[["Angels on horseback","dish/angels-on-horseback"],["Cabinet pudding","dish/cabinet-pudding"],["Clotted cream","dish/clotted-cream"],["Crème anglaise","dish/creme-anglaise"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"],["Maids of honour tart","dish/maids-of-honour-tart"],["Manchester tart","dish/manchester-tart"],["Mock turtle soup","dish/mock-turtle-soup"],["Pork pie","dish/pork-pie"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Windsor soup","dish/windsor-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a9/Pie%2C_mash_and_liquor.jpg/500px-Pie%2C_mash_and_liquor.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Sumit Surai","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pie%2C_mash_and_liquor.jpg"}},"dish/pujol-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pujol-restaurant","n":"Pujol (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Pujol is a Mexican restaurant in Polanco, Miguel Hidalgo, Mexico City. It is owned and headed by chef Enrique Olvera. Pujol's dishes are rooted in traditional Mexican cuisine, including maize-based food, seafood, and tacos, served in a sophisticated presentation through tasting menus or a taco omakase bar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pujol-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pujol_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.c