ms sode, zo(o)de and soot, words referring to the act of boiling or the ingredients being boiled. It is sometimes called Gentse Waterzooi which refers to the Belgian town of Ghent where it originated. The original dish is often made of fish, either freshwater or salt, (known as Viszooitje), though today chicken waterzooi (Kippenwaterzooi) is more common. The most accepted theory is that rivers around Ghent became too polluted and the fish there disappeared. Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor ate the rich dish, even after suffering from gout."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-waterzooi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waterzooi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"]]},{"h":"More from Belgian cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["Algérienne sauce","dish/algerienne-sauce"],["Belgian chocolate","dish/belgian-chocolate"],["Belgo","dish/belgo"],["Bickyburger","dish/bickyburger"],["Boûkète","dish/boukete"],["Flemish stew","dish/flemish-stew"],["Friterie","dish/friterie"],["Hertog Jan (restaurant)","dish/hertog-jan-restaurant"],["Hof van Cleve","dish/hof-van-cleve"],["Liège waffle","dish/liege-waffle"],["Moules-frites","dish/moules-frites"],["Paling in 't groen","dish/paling-in-t-groen"],["Samurai sauce","dish/samurai-sauce"],["Speculoos","dish/speculoos"],["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5e/%28waterzooi%29_%2879743868%29.jpg/500px-%28waterzooi%29_%2879743868%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"ayustety from Tokyo, Japan","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(waterzooi)_(79743868).jpg"}},"cookbook/made-in-bangladesh-recipes-and-stories-from-a-h